{{!
    @template theme_dimensions/competency_classreport

    The class report of report/competency/index.php: one row per learner, one column per course competency, drawn
    by Report Builder (theme_dimensions\reportbuilder\local\systemreports\class_ratings) and handed in whole.

    Above it, what the page must say: that a viewer in no group of a separate-groups course reads no learner, that
    the course has no competency, or that the columns are the first of more. The module theme_dimensions/classratings
    opens core's grading dialogue from a rating cell carrying the hooks and reloads the report's rows when it
    closes; it is armed once per page, from the js block, and finds the report through this root.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * courseid - The course.
    * nogroup - Whether the group rule leaves the viewer no row.
    * nocompetency - Whether the course (or the chosen activity) has no competency.
    * nocompetencynotice - What to say then, plain.
    * capped - Whether the course has more competencies than columns.
    * capnotice - What to say then, plain.
    * report - The report, Report Builder's own markup.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "courseid": 2,
        "nogroup": false,
        "nocompetency": false,
        "nocompetencynotice": "No competency is linked to this course yet.",
        "capped": true,
        "capnotice": "The report shows the first 30 of the course's 32 competencies.",
        "report": "<div class=\"reportbuilder-report\"></div>"
    }
}}
<div class="dim-comp-classreport" data-region="dim-comp-classreport" data-courseid="{{courseid}}">
    {{#nogroup}}
    <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">{{#str}}competency_classreport_nogroup, theme_dimensions{{/str}}</div>
    {{/nogroup}}
    {{#nocompetency}}
    <div class="alert alert-info" role="status">{{nocompetencynotice}}</div>
    {{/nocompetency}}
    {{#capped}}
    <p class="dim-comp-classreport__cap">{{capnotice}}</p>
    {{/capped}}
    {{{report}}}
</div>
{{#js}}
require(['theme_dimensions/classratings'], function(Classratings) {
    Classratings.init();
});
{{/js}}
